# Coding standards

- TypeScript strict. No `any`. Prefer Server Components; add `"use client"` only for interactivity.
- App Router only. `async` page/layout params are `Promise`s in Next 16.
- Tailwind v4 + shadcn `base-nova`. Colors, type, and radius come from `companies.theme` CSS variables — never brand hex or copy in components.
- Every tenant table and query is `company_id`-scoped. Guests are per company, not global.
- Property booking dates: `PropertyBookingCalendar` only on property pages; collection uses `DateSearch` + availability filter (see `booking-calendar.mdc`).
- Direct checkout: `canUseDirectBook` only — no first-time guests on the booking site (`direct-booking.mdc`).
- PriceLabs is the rate brain. AirDNA is market intel. Hospitable is PMS. Do not dual-write prices.
- No `Date.now()` / `Math.random()` during render. Keep impure time in `lib/`.
- Forms: Next.js server actions. Do not return `FormState` from a native `action` unless the form is wired for it.
- Public site uses the service client after tenant resolve. Staff auth is Better Auth, then service role.
- Lint (`eslint-config-next` core-web-vitals), Prettier, and `tsc --noEmit` must pass. PRs get GitHub CI plus Cursor Bugbot (`cursor review` if it did not auto-run).
